#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tumor_immunity_analysis
#
# The governing rule of this repository: CODE travels through git, DATA never
# does. Every dataset lives on TACC under $SCRATCH. Nothing in data/ is ever
# committed, from either side of the sync.
#
# The directories themselves ARE tracked, via .gitkeep, so that a fresh clone
# on a laptop has exactly the same paths as the TACC checkout. Code can then
# hardcode `data/raw/<GSEID>/` and be correct in both places -- empty locally,
# populated on Vista.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- Data trees: structure tracked, contents never -------------------------
# Ignore everything inside, then re-admit the .gitkeep that holds the dir.
data/**
!data/
!data/*/
!data/**/.gitkeep

#--- Claude Code local settings --------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

#--- Vendor bundles from colleagues ----------------------------------------
# ImmuCA/ and scSurvival-extend/ are their authors' code, extracted here only so
# it can be read. The authoritative copies live on Vista under data/ (212 GB and
# 6.9 GB respectively) and both trees carry notebooks with embedded outputs that
# run to several MB each. Read them locally; never commit them.
/ImmuCA/
/scSurvival-extend/
*.tar.gz

#--- Slides -----------------------------------------------------------------
# No decks in git, generated or otherwise. The colleagues' are 16-22 MB, and
# ours is regenerable: scripts/make_figures.py + scripts/make_deck.py rebuild it
# from the numbers recorded in docs/background.md, and those scripts ARE tracked.
# The figures themselves (PNG, ~150 KB each) are tracked, so the content is in
# history even though the container is not.
*.pptx

#--- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

#--- PENCIL's own run artefacts --------------------------------------------
#--- Results: NEVER in git ---------------------------------------------------
# Results are produced on Vista and travel by scp, not by git. Committing them
# makes `git pull` on Vista collide with the very files that generated them --
# which is exactly what happened at d999c85, where ~50 downloaded CSVs were
# committed and the next pull aborted on "untracked working tree files would be
# overwritten". The directory itself stays, via .gitkeep.
results/**
!results/
!results/.gitkeep

# PENCIL also writes ./results/<data_name>/py/<expr_id>/{report.txt,*.csv,*.pdf}
# relative to the CWD. Covered by the rule above; noted here so the directories
# are not mistaken for ours.
